<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antioch-on-the-Orontes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antioch-on-the-Orontes was a city founded around 300 BCE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucus-i-nicator">Seleucus I Nicator</a>, named after his father Antiochus. It became the main royal capital and administrative centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Its name distinguishes it from the many other cities called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> that the Seleucids founded.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antioch-on-the-orontes.jpg" alt="Antioch-on-the-Orontes" width="320" height="388" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UndercoverClassicist · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antioch_on_the_Orontes_en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
